#!/usr/local/bin/dyalogscript
⍝ Phase 9: locks in the four previously-open Fff cover-layer parser
⍝ shapes (see docs/adr/0001-architecture-decisions.md ADR D15 and
⍝ TODO.md's "Fff cover layer" section) — auto-broadened queries,
⍝ grep's path-only fallback, output_mode:'files_with_matches'/'count',
⍝ and multi-file/large-context grouping under real pagination load.
⍝
⍝ Loaded from this worktree's own src/ (not the D:\devel\mcp-client
⍝ root the sibling 01-08 tests hardcode) since this branch's fixes
⍝ only exist here until merged — this agent works only inside its
⍝ worktree. Connect's search target is this same worktree, for the
⍝ same reason (it's "this repo" for this branch's purposes, per the
⍝ task's own instruction to search "this repo itself").
⎕IO←1
⎕FIX'file://D:/devel/mcp-client/.claude/worktrees/agent-a9c43dc899d370691/src/Shell.dyalog'
⎕FIX'file://D:/devel/mcp-client/.claude/worktrees/agent-a9c43dc899d370691/src/JsonRpc.dyalog'
⎕FIX'file://D:/devel/mcp-client/.claude/worktrees/agent-a9c43dc899d370691/src/Mcp.dyalog'
⎕FIX'file://D:/devel/mcp-client/.claude/worktrees/agent-a9c43dc899d370691/src/Fff.dyalog'

h←Fff.Connect'D:\devel\mcp-client\.claude\worktrees\agent-a9c43dc899d370691'

nFail←0

⍝ --- 1. Auto-broadened query header --------------------------------
⍝ "0 matches for '<q>'. Auto-broadened to '<q2>':" — Shown/Total must
⍝ reflect the broadened result's real count (not the leading, always-
⍝ 0 exact-match count), Broadened must carry <q2>, and the broadened
⍝ results must still parse as Files. The second word is built by
⍝ concatenation (not written contiguously anywhere in this file, this
⍝ line included) so it names a real, rare identifier — exactly 2
⍝ occurrences in this tree, both in one file — without this test file
⍝ itself becoming a 3rd occurrence and pushing the retry over fff's
⍝ own ≤10-matches threshold for accepting a broadened retry.
rareWord←'_StripDef','Tag'
r1←h Fff.Grep'zzzznonexistentword12345 ',rareWord
⎕←'broadened: Shown=',(⍕r1.Shown),' Total=',(⍕r1.Total),' Broadened=[',r1.Broadened,'] files=',⍕≢r1.Files
:If (r1.Broadened≢rareWord)∨(r1.Shown=0)∨(r1.Shown≠r1.Total)∨(0=≢r1.Files)
    ⎕←'FAIL: expected a non-zero Shown/Total, Broadened=rareWord, and non-empty Files'
    nFail←nFail+1
:EndIf
⍝ The broadened results must parse as genuine Files, not garbage —
⍝ every Path must be non-blank and not itself a stray match/context
⍝ line (the exact grouping bug ADR D12 fixed, re-checked here for the
⍝ auto-broadened shape specifically).
:If ~∧/0≠≢¨r1.Files.Path
    ⎕←'FAIL: broadened result has a blank Path'
    nFail←nFail+1
:EndIf

⍝ Same header, under output_mode:'files_with_matches' and 'count' —
⍝ server.rs re-invokes GrepFormatter with the *original* output_mode
⍝ for the broadened retry, so the embedded text is mode-formatted too.
r1b←h Fff.Grep(('zzzznonexistentword12345 ',rareWord)(output_mode:'files_with_matches'))
⎕←'broadened+files_with_matches: Shown=',(⍕r1b.Shown),' Broadened=[',r1b.Broadened,'] files=',⍕≢r1b.Files
:If (r1b.Broadened≢rareWord)∨(0=≢r1b.Files)
    ⎕←'FAIL: broadened+files_with_matches lost Broadened or Files'
    nFail←nFail+1
:EndIf

r1c←h Fff.Grep(('zzzznonexistentword12345 ',rareWord)(output_mode:'count'))
⎕←'broadened+count: Shown=',(⍕r1c.Shown),' Broadened=[',r1c.Broadened,'] counts=',⍕≢r1c.Counts
:If (r1c.Broadened≢rareWord)∨(0=≢r1c.Counts)
    ⎕←'FAIL: broadened+count lost Broadened or Counts'
    nFail←nFail+1
:EndIf

⍝ --- 2. Path-only fallback ------------------------------------------
⍝ "0 content matches. But there is a relevant file path: <p>" — <p>
⍝ must land in SuggestedPath, not be silently dropped. A query that
⍝ resembles a real filename closely enough for fff's fuzzy file-path
⍝ scorer, but whose content never occurs verbatim (so grep's own
⍝ content search and fuzzy-line fallback both come up empty first) —
⍝ reversed (as test/06's no-hit query already does) so this file
⍝ doesn't itself become a fuzzy self-match once it's part of the
⍝ searched tree: plain concatenation wasn't enough, since fff's fuzzy
⍝ fallback matches on similarity, not just exact substrings, and
⍝ still found this very line.
pathQuery←⌽'golaydlCcpRnosJ/qzqzz'
r2←h Fff.Grep pathQuery
⎕←'path-only fallback: Shown=',(⍕r2.Shown),' SuggestedPath=[',r2.SuggestedPath,']'
:If (0≠r2.Shown)∨(0≠≢r2.Files)∨(0=≢r2.SuggestedPath)∨(~∨/'JsonRpcCl.dyalog'⍷r2.SuggestedPath)
    ⎕←'FAIL: expected Shown=0, no Files, and a SuggestedPath naming JsonRpcCl.dyalog'
    nFail←nFail+1
:EndIf

⍝ --- 3. output_mode:'files_with_matches' ----------------------------
⍝ Never has a "N/Total matches" header (Shown/Total default to the
⍝ file count) and, unlike every other mode, path lines can carry a
⍝ genuine "[def]" tag — must be stripped into IsDef, not left riding
⍝ along in Path.
r3←h Fff.Grep('Namespace'(maxResults:10 ⋄ output_mode:'files_with_matches'))
⎕←'files_with_matches: Shown=',(⍕r3.Shown),' Total=',(⍕r3.Total),' files=',(⍕≢r3.Files),' anyDef=',⍕∨/r3.Files.IsDef
:If (r3.Shown≠r3.Total)∨(r3.Shown≠≢r3.Files)∨(0=≢r3.Files)
    ⎕←'FAIL: expected Shown=Total=file count for files_with_matches'
    nFail←nFail+1
:EndIf
:If ∨/∊'[def]'∘⍷¨r3.Files.Path
    ⎕←'FAIL: a Path still carries its raw [def] tag — should be stripped into IsDef'
    nFail←nFail+1
:EndIf

⍝ --- 4. output_mode:'count' -----------------------------------------
⍝ One "{path}: {count}" line per file, no header, no per-line Matches
⍝ at all — Counts is the mode-specific field; Files stays empty. Also
⍝ locks in the _ToInt fix (ADR D15): Counts.Count, gathered via dot
⍝ notation across several namespace refs, used to come out nested and
⍝ DOMAIN ERROR any :If that tested it directly.
r4←h Fff.Grep('Namespace'(maxResults:10 ⋄ output_mode:'count'))
⎕←'count: Shown=',(⍕r4.Shown),' counts=',(⍕≢r4.Counts),' Files=',⍕≢r4.Files
:If (0≠≢r4.Files)∨(0=≢r4.Counts)∨(r4.Shown≠+/r4.Counts.Count)
    ⎕←'FAIL: expected empty Files, non-empty Counts, Shown = sum of counts'
    nFail←nFail+1
:EndIf
:If ~∧/0<r4.Counts.Count
    ⎕←'FAIL: every Counts entry should have a positive Count'
    nFail←nFail+1
:EndIf

⍝ --- 5. Multi-file / large-context grouping stress ------------------
⍝ A far larger context than the 1/2 used elsewhere, against a query
⍝ with many hits spread over several files — re-checks the file-
⍝ changes-when-path-line-seen grouping logic (ADR D12) doesn't
⍝ corrupt under real pagination load. (Also verified by hand against
⍝ the much larger D:\devel\fff source tree — see ADR D15 — but that
⍝ tree isn't guaranteed present in every environment this test runs
⍝ in, so the committed test stays scoped to this repo.)
r5←h Fff.Grep(('_Pa','rse')(context:4 ⋄ maxResults:40))
⎕←'stress: Shown=',(⍕r5.Shown),' Total=',(⍕r5.Total),' files=',(⍕≢r5.Files),' Cursor=[',r5.Cursor,']'
kinds←(∊r5.Files.Matches).Kind
⎕←'kind tally: Match=',(⍕+/'Match'∘≡¨kinds),' Context=',(⍕+/'Context'∘≡¨kinds),' DefContext=',(⍕+/'DefContext'∘≡¨kinds)
:If 0=≢r5.Files
    ⎕←'FAIL: expected at least one file for a ''_Parse'' grep with context:4'
    nFail←nFail+1
:EndIf
:If ~∧/0≠≢¨r5.Files.Path
    ⎕←'FAIL: stress probe produced a blank Path — file/match grouping likely corrupted'
    nFail←nFail+1
:EndIf
⍝ Every Path must look like a path, not a leaked match/context line —
⍝ i.e. never start with a digit followed by ':'/'-'/'|' (_ParseMatchLine's
⍝ own annotated-line shapes).
:For f :In r5.Files
    ⍝ A real path re-run through _ParseMatchLine must never itself
    ⍝ look like an annotated line (kind='').
    (kind num txt)←Fff._ParseMatchLine' ',f.Path
    :If 0≠≢kind
        ⎕←'FAIL: Path looks like a leaked match/context line: [',f.Path,']'
        nFail←nFail+1
    :EndIf
:EndFor

⎕←'nFail=',⍕nFail
:If nFail≠0
    ⎕←'FAIL: ',(⍕nFail),' check(s) failed'
:Else
    ⎕←'all checks passed'
:EndIf

Fff.Disconnect h
⎕OFF
